#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
iceberg_packer.py -- dedupe, extract, pack, archive.

For one source folder (default: STANDARD_PHYSICS_ICEBERG):

  1. Hash everything; exact duplicates are DELETED (first copy kept).
  2. TEXT: extract whatever text is extractable (txt/json/code, pdf, docx, htm/mhtml,
     images via OCR, audio/video via faster-whisper) and pack it into
        ~2.3 MB dated .txt packets  -> NoteFeed
        ~23  MB dated .json packets -> Git-O-Matic
  3. VISUAL: images, pdf, htm/html/mhtml, tex (compiled), office docs are combined into
        ~2.3 MB pdf packets -> NoteFeed
        ~23  MB pdf packets -> Git-O-Matic
  4. SQUARE images (aspect within tolerance of 1:1) are saved individually -> Git-O-Matic
  5. If every output verifies under its size cap, the whole source folder is moved into
     <ARCHIVE_ROOT>/<datestamp>_<foldername>/ (copy -> verify -> delete original, file by
     file) and the original folder is left empty.

Nothing destructive happens until the very end, and only if verification passed.
A failed or interrupted run leaves the source exactly as it was (duplicates included).

Hard caps (strictly below): NoteFeed 2.5 MB per file, Git-O-Matic 25 MB per file
(decimal MB, same convention as split_pdf_24mb.py).

Optional libraries (each missing one just disables its tier; startup prints what's found):
    python -m pip install -U pypdf pillow img2pdf python-docx pytesseract pymupdf faster-whisper
    Tesseract OCR binary (for pytesseract), Edge/Chrome (htm->pdf), lualatex/pdflatex (tex->pdf),
    LibreOffice 'soffice' (office->pdf).

Examples:
    python iceberg_packer.py                       # asks for folder + recurse, uses defaults
    python iceberg_packer.py --source "D:\\other\\folder" --recurse
    python iceberg_packer.py --dry-run             # inventory + dedupe report only
    python iceberg_packer.py --tiers all           # include audio/video transcription
"""
